  "claim_short": "arXiv 2305.12873 Ermakoff condition t g(t)/g(e^t). Full construction: for every a>0, put c=log a, choose A>max(0,c), E0=exp A, and m=(A-c)/(exp A-A). Seed h(x)=m x on [0,E0], extend across iterated-exponential intervals by h(y)=h(log y)+log y-c, and set g(t)=exp(h(log t)). The construction is continuous and strictly increasing, g(1)=1, and t g(t)/g(exp t)=a exactly for every t>=exp A. Hence every positive finite...",
